"[2511.08939v1] TransactionGPT (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08939v1)\nciteturn5949view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08939v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025 (this version), latest version 2 Mar 2026 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:TransactionGPT\nL10: Authors:cite6†Yingtong Dou , cite7†Zhimeng Jiang , cite8†Tianyi Zhang , cite9†Mingzhi Hu , cite10†Zhichao Xu , cite11†Shubham Jain , cite12†Uday Singh Saini , cite13†Xiran Fan , cite14†Jiarui Sun , cite15†Menghai Pan , cite16†Junpeng Wang , cite17†Xin Dai , cite18†Liang Wang , cite19†Chin-Chia Michael Yeh , cite20†Yujie Fan , cite21†Vineeth Rakesh , cite22†Huiyuan Chen , cite23†Mangesh Bendre , cite24†Zhongfang Zhuang , cite25†Xiaoting Li , cite26†Prince Aboagye , cite27†Vivian Lai , cite28†Minghua Xu , cite29†Hao Yang , cite30†Yiwei Cai , cite31†Mahashweta Das , cite32†Yuzhong Chen L11: View a PDF of the paper titled TransactionGPT, by Yingtong Dou and 26 other authors\nL12: \nL13: cite33†View PDF cite34†HTML (experimental) L14: > Abstract:We present TransactionGPT (TGPT), a foundation model for consumer transaction data within one of world's largest payment networks. TGPT is designed to understand and generate transaction trajectories while simultaneously supporting a variety of downstream prediction and classification tasks. We introduce a novel 3D-Transformer architecture specifically tailored for capturing the complex dynamics in payment transaction data.\nL15: This architecture incorporates design innovations that enhance modality fusion and computational efficiency, while seamlessly enabling joint optimization with downstream objectives. Trained on billion-scale real-world transactions, TGPT significantly improves downstream classification performance against a competitive production model and exhibits advantages over baselines in generating future transactions.\nL16: We conduct extensive empirical evaluations utilizing a diverse collection of company transaction datasets spanning multiple downstream tasks, thereby enabling a thorough assessment of TGPT's effectiveness and efficiency in comparison to established methodologies. Furthermore, we examine the incorporation of LLM-derived embeddings within TGPT and benchmark its performance against fine-tuned LLMs, demonstrating that TGPT achieves superior predictive accuracy as well as faster training and inference.\nL17: We anticipate that the architectural innovations and practical guidelines from this work will advance foundation models for transaction-like data and catalyze future research in this emerging field.\nL18: Comments:  | Technical Report\nL19: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite35†arXiv:2511.08939 [cs.LG]\nL21:    | (or cite36†arXiv:2511.08939v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL22:    | cite37†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.08939†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Yingtong Dou [cite38†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 03:31:34 UTC (4,140 KB)\nL27: cite5†[v2] Mon, 2 Mar 2026 22:48:45 UTC (4,082 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled TransactionGPT, by Yingtong Dou and 26 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite33†View PDF L36:   * cite34†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite39†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite40†view license†creativecommons.org L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.LG\nL43: \nL44: cite41†< prev