.arxiv.org · cite78†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L163: \nL164: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.09085v1] Context-Aware Dynamic Chunking for Streaming Tibetan Speech Recognition (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09085v1)\nciteturn5949view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09085v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:Context-Aware Dynamic Chunking for Streaming Tibetan Speech Recognition\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Chao Wang , cite6†Yuqing Cai , cite7†Renzeng Duojie , cite8†Jin Zhang , cite9†Yutong Liu , cite10†Nyima Tashi L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Context-Aware Dynamic Chunking for Streaming Tibetan Speech Recognition, by Chao Wang and 4 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF cite12†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:In this work, we propose a streaming speech recognition framework for Amdo Tibetan, built upon a hybrid CTC/Atten-tion architecture with a context-aware dynamic chunking mechanism. The proposed strategy adaptively adjusts chunk widths based on encoding states, enabling flexible receptive fields, cross-chunk information exchange, and robust adaptation to varying speaking rates, thereby alleviating the context truncation problem of fixed-chunk methods.\nL17: To further capture the linguistic characteristics of Tibetan, we construct a lexicon grounded in its orthographic principles, providing linguistically motivated modeling units. During decoding, an external language model is integrated to enhance semantic consistency and improve recognition of long sentences.\nL18: Experimental results show that the proposed framework achieves a word error rate (WER) of 6.23% on the test set, yielding a 48.15% relative improvement over the fixed-chunk baseline, while significantly reducing recognition latency and maintaining performance close to global decoding.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite13†arXiv:2511.09085 [cs.CL]\nL21:    | (or cite14†arXiv:2511.09085v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL22:    | cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09085†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Chao Wang [cite16†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 08:00:52 UTC (184 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Context-Aware Dynamic Chunking for Streaming Tibetan Speech Recognition, by Chao Wang and 4 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite11†View PDF L35:   * cite12†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite17†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite18†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.CL\nL42: \nL43: cite19†< prev |   cite20†next > L44: \nL45: cite21†new | cite22†recent | cite23†2025-11 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite24†cs L50: \nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite25†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite26†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite27†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL70: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL73: \nL74: Bibliographic Explorer (cite28†What is the Explorer?†in